# Hadoop's FileUtil.unTarUsingTar builds a shell command by appending
# segments to a StringBuffer and hands the result to `bash -c`, so every
# shell metacharacter in the assembled string is live. The non-gzipped
# branch appends FileUtil.makeSecureShellPath(inFile) straight into the
# command with no surrounding quotes; the gzipped branch and the `cd`
# segment both wrap the same helper's result in a literal `'...'` pair.
# makeSecureShellPath only escapes embedded single quotes
# (`replace("'", "'\\''")`), and that escaping holds only when the caller
# also wraps the result in single quotes -- exactly what the unquoted
# branch skips, so an archive path containing metacharacters reaches the
# shell (CWE-78, CWE-88). The fix (cae749b0, HADOOP-18136) hoists
# `final String source = "'" + FileUtil.makeSecureShellPath(inFile) +
# "'";` and appends `source` in both branches, so the previously-unquoted
# operand gets the same wrapping.
#
# Vocabulary. bindings.java.shellCommandAssemblyWithoutQuoting reads four
# function-scope facts, each POSIX or JDK vocabulary: a `bash`/`sh` string
# literal and a `-c` string literal (the interpreter-invocation array
# handed to the executor), an `append` call (the StringBuilder/StringBuffer
# assembly idiom), and the absence of a string literal whose entire content
# is one apostrophe -- the POSIX single-quote wrapping, which appears in the
# fixed revision as the `"'"` operands of the hoisted assignment and in
# `.append("'")` spellings generally, while a quote glued into a longer
# segment literal (`"' && "`) is not that literal and does not suppress,
# correctly, because it quotes its own segment rather than the operand
# appended next to it. The judgement is code.CommandLineAssemblyReview
# (VYQL-INJ-053), whose review condition is this shape verbatim; no engine
# change. Assembly by plain concatenation is a documented false-negative
# residual: its safe spelling delegates the quoting to a helper
# (bashQuote), whose body is outside the launching function's context.
#
# Discrimination, --cache off scans of the org.apache.hadoop.fs subtree
# (296 files) at each revision, identical across repeated runs: 40 findings
# with exactly 1 VYQL-INJ-053 on cae749b0^ (FileUtil.java:888,
# unTarUsingTar), 39 findings and 0 VYQL-INJ-053 on cae749b0 -- the
# baseline rulesets differ by nothing else. On the wider hadoop-common
# main tree (1113 files): 514 with exactly the one VYQL-INJ-053 at
# cae749b0^ against 513 and none at cae749b0, stable over three baseline
# runs. Exhaustive grep puts both a `bash`/`sh` literal and a `-c` literal
# in exactly five files of that tree; the four besides FileUtil stay
# unreported for reasons the enumeration confirms: DF quotes its operand
# in-command (`... + dirPath + "'"`), Shell assembles by concatenation with
# bashQuote-delegated quoting, ShellCommandFencer's command arrives from a
# helper with no in-function assembly, and ShellBasedIdMapping's constant
# echo commands have no dynamic operand.
#
# verify_current_expected: fixed

test "rank1157: the escaped path is appended into the bash command with no surrounding quotes"
  lang java
  file FileUtil.java
  expect VYQL-INJ-053
  expect_review code.CommandLineAssemblyReview
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.hadoop.fs;

  public class FileUtil {
    private static void unTarUsingTar(File inFile, File untarDir, boolean gzipped) throws IOException {
      StringBuffer untarCommand = new StringBuffer();
      if (gzipped) {
        untarCommand.append(" gzip -dc '")
            .append(FileUtil.makeSecureShellPath(inFile))
            .append("' | (");
      }
      untarCommand.append("cd '")
          .append(FileUtil.makeSecureShellPath(untarDir))
          .append("' && ")
          .append("tar -xf ");

      if (gzipped) {
        untarCommand.append(" -)");
      } else {
        untarCommand.append(FileUtil.makeSecureShellPath(inFile));
      }
      String[] shellCmd = { "bash", "-c", untarCommand.toString() };
      ShellCommandExecutor shexec = new ShellCommandExecutor(shellCmd);
      shexec.execute();
      int exitcode = shexec.getExitCode();
      if (exitcode != 0) {
        throw new IOException("Error untarring file " + inFile +
                    ". Tar process exited with exit code " + exitcode);
      }
    }

    public static String makeSecureShellPath(File file) throws IOException {
      return makeShellPath(file, false).replace("'", "'\\''");
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1157: both branches append a source wrapped in single quotes"
  lang java
  file FileUtil.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-053
  reject_review code.CommandLineAssemblyReview
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.hadoop.fs;

  public class FileUtil {
    private static void unTarUsingTar(File inFile, File untarDir, boolean gzipped) throws IOException {
      StringBuffer untarCommand = new StringBuffer();
      final String source = "'" + FileUtil.makeSecureShellPath(inFile) + "'";
      if (gzipped) {
        untarCommand.append(" gzip -dc ")
            .append(source)
            .append(" | (");
      }
      untarCommand.append("cd '")
          .append(FileUtil.makeSecureShellPath(untarDir))
          .append("' && ")
          .append("tar -xf ");

      if (gzipped) {
        untarCommand.append(" -)");
      } else {
        untarCommand.append(source);
      }
      String[] shellCmd = { "bash", "-c", untarCommand.toString() };
      ShellCommandExecutor shexec = new ShellCommandExecutor(shellCmd);
      shexec.execute();
      int exitcode = shexec.getExitCode();
      if (exitcode != 0) {
        throw new IOException("Error untarring file " + inFile +
            ". Tar process exited with exit code " + exitcode);
      }
    }

    public static String makeSecureShellPath(File file) throws IOException {
      return makeShellPath(file, false).replace("'", "'\\''");
    }
  }
  ```
